  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_geo",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 762
        },
        "text": "UV (tiled per layer), object height, world normal and the mesh vertex colour."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_weights",
        "position": {
          "x": 988,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1986
        },
        "text": "`snow = smoothstep(line, line + soft, y)`, `rock = smoothstep(slope, slope + 0.25, 1 − N·up)`, `dirt = smoothstep(0.45, 0.65, fbm) × amount`, grass = 1. Painted vertex colours replace the whole vector when **Use Vertex Colors** is on."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fbbf24",
        "id": "note_fetch",
        "position": {
          "x": 988,
          "y": 1079
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1154
        },
        "text": "Each layer is sampled once at the tiled UV. The albedo luminance (`0.3 R + 0.59 G + 0.11 B`) doubles as the layer height for the height blend."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_blend",
        "position": {
          "x": 3178,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 848
        },
        "text": "The **Height Blend (4 layers)** kit sharpens the raw weights with the layer heights and normalises them."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_mix",
        "position": {
          "x": 4230,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 848
        },
        "text": "`albedo = Σ wᵢ × layerᵢ`; smoothness blends towards the snow value by the snow weight."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 5282,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Blended albedo and smoothness."
      }
    ],
