            "text": "**Height blend** — `score = weight + height`; the winning score `m = max(score)` defines a window of size *depth*: `b = saturate(score − (m − depth))`, result `b / Σb`.\nPeaks of a layer (stones, grass tufts) poke through its neighbours instead of fading linearly, which is what makes painted terrain look natural. Four layers cost one add, three maxes, one subtract, one saturate and one divide."
          }
        ],
